  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 310 PM EDT Fri Sep 18 2026\n\n- Heavy Rain Likely Across Southwest Lower Michigan This Weekend\n\nWe have gone ahead an issued a Flood Watch for Allegan, Barry, Van\nBuren, Kalamazoo and Calhoun Counties. These are the counties that\nwe have more confidence in seeing the higher amounts (2-4 inches)\nby Sunday morning. 1 to 2 inch amounts are likely outside of those\n5 counties. \n\nAloft, a zonal upper flow will be in place through Sunday with\nnumerous shortwaves working east through the flow over the Great\nLakes region. Down at the surface weak low pressure will move from\nthe Central Plains into the Ohio Valley. An overrunning situation\nsets up as south/southwest flow rides northeast over cooler air at\nthe surface over Lower Michigan. This lift will result in\nprecipitation that lasts the better part of 24 hours from near\nmidnight tonight to midnight Saturday night. The repeated training\nof echoes over Southwest Lower Michigan will result in heavy\nrain. Forcing will also be provided by the right front quad of an\nupper jet to our north that will lead to a low level jet response\nthat stays fairly steady state (aimed at our area) for the better\npart of 24 hours. PWAT values over Southern Lower Michigan will be\nin the 1.75 to 2.00 inch range which is very high for this time of\nyear. Surface dew points will not be as high (in the 60s F), but\nthis is still high for this time of year as well. Bottom line...we\nare looking at rounds of heavy rain that will likely lead to\nponding of water in low lying areas and urban centers as well.\nRises on area rivers and streams will occur. At this time we are\nnot expecting widespread river flooding in terms of reaching flood\nstage but we will be monitoring closely. \n\n- Mainly Dry Next Week After Weekend Rain\n\nWe are looking at mainly dry weather next week for the bulk of the\narea as Canadian high pressure sags in from the north. The\nquestion mark will be Southern Lower Michigan which may remain\njust close enough to low level moisture as we sit beneath an upper\ntrough.\n\n- Cooler Than Normal Weather Much of the 7 Day Forecast\n\nCooler than normal weather is expected through the period with\nhighs in the 60s much of the time. Rain this weekend and then\ncooler air moving in at 850mb will be the reason for the cooler\nweather. 850mb temperatures in the teens C this weekend will cool\ninto the single digit C range next week. Normal highs are in the\nlower 70s for the most part and we should be below that much of\nthe next 7 days. It will feel like fall.",
